[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-10-09T14:36:29Z"
 content="""
This is not macOS specific. The directory special remote requires a
directory= parameter be given to initremote. That is to support things like
a directory special remote that points to a USB drive that moves between
several computers. The mount point of the drive can be different on each
computer, and so each place the directory special remote is enabled it
needs the directory= to be specified.

I don't really see any point in using git-remote-annex with a directory
special remote. You can just as well use a bare git repository. 

But anyway, if you pass the directory= parameter to enableremote, it does work.

BTW, it's not necessary to run enableremote after initremote. You can just
run initremote --with-url.
"""]]
